6 Notice of this appeal was sent to respondent and Ld. counsel for respondent appeared and filed written reply to the present appeal stating therein that the appeal under reply is not verified by the appellants in view of the provisions of CPC hence the appeal is liable to be dismissed on this ground; that the present appeal is liable to be dismissed in view of illustration (b) of Section 101 of The Indian Evidence Act 1872; that it is settled law that in Mohd. Afzal Chand And Anr vs Zulfikar Ahmed on 11 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/41016505/
4 a suit for possession, the burden is on the plaintiff to make out his title and entitlement to possession and he cannot succeed on the basis of weakness in title or right to possession of the defendant; that a person wants to recover the possession of land from occupier on the ground that he is the owner of it, he must have proved his ownership; that appellants have not proved their ownership hence appeal is liable to be dismissed with cost; that the contents of written statement,
evidence by way of affidavit of DW1 to DW5 and contents of Ex.DW1/1, Ex.DW1/2 and Ex.DW1/3 (colly.) be read as part and parcel of the present reply which are not repeated herein for the sake of brevity; that the suit property is situated within the jurisdiction of North-East District; that the appellants have no locus standi to file the suit and present appeal is liable to be dismissed with cost;
